  "_costModelNote": "Each entry is the MOST EXPENSIVE resolution/channel for its model (fail-safe direction, phase 1.3) — price-breakeven.ts's modelBreakEven keys strictly on matrix.modelId (COST_MODEL.find, single match), so a model with per-resolution COGS cannot have more than one entry here. This is a real shape limitation of price-breakeven.ts, reported per phase 1.3 rather than silently working around it: it means the break-even guard checks ONE reference config per model, not every priced row. `fallbackCostPerCredit` is null everywhere — the retired file's fallback numbers all cited the wrong workbook column (data-audit finding C3: 'Тарифы!AE##' is a MARGIN column; the stored values actually came from 'AD') and v14's per-model channel table gives exactly one $/unit figure per model, not a primary+fallback pair, so there is no v14-sourced replacement to re-cite. Video entries priced 'per CLIP' in v14 (Veo) carry cogsUsdPerUnit as (clipCost ÷ refClipSeconds) — a $/second EQUIVALENT — so price-breakeven.ts's existing `cogsUsdPerUnit × refClipSeconds` formula (unchanged, out of this brief's scope) recovers the correct per-clip cost instead of the 8× overcount data-audit finding C4 flagged (the retired file's Veo numbers were ALSO stored this way, just wrong-valued; C4's warning was about resyncing the VALUE without preserving this semantic — this file avoids that trap by construction)."
